<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Last updated: 1 October 2026</p>
<p>This policy explains how Notae handles personal information when you use <a href="https://notae.esquarenews.tech/">notae.esquarenews.tech</a>, its workspace features, and connected services. For privacy questions or requests, contact Errol Schmidt at <a href="mailto:errol@esquarenews.com.au">errol@esquarenews.com.au</a>.</p>

<h2>Information we collect</h2>
<p>We collect account and profile information you provide, such as your email address, name, avatar, preferences, and account credentials. We also store content you add to Notae: notes, documents, grids, tasks, files, comments, calendars, meeting recordings and transcripts, and AI conversations. That content may contain personal information about you or other people.</p>
<p>We process workspace membership, permissions, subscription and payment status, usage and activity records, audit history, and technical information needed to operate the service, such as request logs, device or browser information, and notification subscriptions. Payment processing is handled by Stripe; Notae stores billing references and subscription information rather than full payment-card details.</p>

<h2>How we use information</h2>
<p>We use information to authenticate accounts, provide and synchronise workspace features, manage permissions and subscriptions, send requested notifications and service messages, respond to support requests, prevent abuse, troubleshoot faults, and understand service usage. Workspace analytics may be enabled by workspace settings. We do not sell personal information or use workspace content for targeted advertising.</p>

<h2>Google Calendar and other connections</h2>
<p>Connecting Google Calendar is optional. With your authorisation, Notae reads your calendar list and event information, including titles, descriptions, times, locations, attendees, and identifiers where supplied by Google. Notae stores synchronised calendar and event information to display your schedule, support search, and connect events to workspace content. When you create, edit, or delete an event in a writable connected calendar, Notae sends the corresponding change to Google.</p>
<p>Calendar event access and read-only calendar-list access support these features. Existing OAuth grants may include broader Calendar permission; Notae uses that access only for the calendar features described here. We store access and refresh tokens to maintain the connection; those credentials are encrypted in the application database. Calendar visibility depends on whether you select a personal or shared workspace connection and on workspace permissions.</p>
<p>Connected calendar information may also be used as context for enabled Notae AI features, such as answering questions about your schedule or workspace. Relevant information may be sent to the configured AI provider to deliver those features. We do not use Google user data to train general-purpose AI or machine-learning models.</p>
<p>Notae's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a> and the <a href="https://developers.google.com/workspace/workspace-api-user-data-developer-policy">Google Workspace API User Data and Developer Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Transfers are limited to providing or improving the user-facing features you use, security, legal requirements, or a permitted business transfer with appropriate consent. Human access to Google data is limited to your affirmative agreement, necessary security investigations, legal obligations, or aggregated and anonymised internal operations permitted by those policies.</p>
<p>You can disconnect a calendar in Notae's calendar settings and revoke Google access through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">your Google Account connections</a>. Revocation prevents further authorised access but does not itself delete content already copied into notes, grids, exports, or backups. Contact us if you want retained information deleted. Other optional calendar connections, including iCloud and calendar feeds, process the credentials and event information needed for the connection you select.</p>

<h2>AI and meeting features</h2>
<p>AI features process your prompts and relevant workspace context through configured service providers, including OpenAI where enabled. Meeting features can process recordings, transcripts, participant details, and summaries. Only record or upload meetings when you have the necessary permission from participants. Provider processing is subject to their applicable terms and privacy practices. Avoid submitting information you are not authorised to share.</p>

<h2>Who can receive information</h2>
<p>Your content may be available to workspace members according to their permissions. Public sharing links and exports can disclose content to their recipients; check sharing settings before publishing. Workspace administrators can manage membership and workspace settings.</p>
<p>Service providers may process information needed for hosting, storage, email delivery, payments, AI, and connected services. We may disclose information where legally required, to protect people or the service, or as part of a business transfer subject to appropriate privacy protections. Providers may process information outside Australia, including in the United States. Locations depend on the provider and the connection used; contact us for information relevant to your account.</p>

<h2>Cookies, security, and retention</h2>
<p>Notae uses session cookies and browser storage for sign-in, security, preferences, and application operation. Browser notification permissions control web push notifications. You can manage cookies and permissions in your browser; disabling essential cookies may prevent sign-in.</p>
<p>We use access controls and encryption for stored integration credentials. No online service can guarantee absolute security. Keep your account credentials and API tokens private and report suspected unauthorised access promptly.</p>
<p>We retain information while it is needed to provide the service and for legitimate security, operational, legal, and accounting purposes. Deletion may not immediately remove information from backups or audit records. Shared workspace records may remain where other members require them. We do not promise a fixed deletion period; contact us to discuss your request and any required retention.</p>

<h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
<p>You can update your profile, adjust sharing and notification settings, disconnect integrations, and export workspace content where your permissions and plan allow. Account settings include an account deletion request. You can also email us to request access, correction, or deletion of personal information, or to raise a privacy complaint. We may verify your identity and explain any lawful limits on a request.</p>
<p>We aim to acknowledge privacy complaints promptly and respond within 30 days. If a complaint remains unresolved, you can contact the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>, where applicable.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We will publish updates here with a revised date and provide additional notice of material changes where appropriate. Our <%= link_to "Terms of Use", terms_of_use_path %> explain the conditions for using Notae.</p>
